 "intro": "Vocabulary for documents, appointments, forms, fees and deadlines, and how to say that something is necessary.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "DNI",
   "significado": "Spanish national identity card",
   "pron": "de-E-ne-I",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "They are the initials of «Documento Nacional de Identidad». It is read letter by letter: de, ene, i.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "renovar",
   "significado": "to renew",
   "pron": "rre-no-BAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The o becomes ue: «renuevo», «renueva», but «renovamos». You renew a passport or a licence.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "solicitar",
   "significado": "to apply for; to request",
   "pron": "so-li-thi-TAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is more formal than «pedir». You can «solicitar» a grant, a visa or an appointment.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cita previa",
   "significado": "prior appointment",
   "pron": "THI-ta PRE-bya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The usual verbs are «pedir» and «coger» cita previa, usually online or by phone.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "impreso",
   "significado": "form",
   "pron": "im-PRE-so",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a printed paper you fill in with your details. You say «rellenar un impreso».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ventanilla",
   "significado": "counter; service window",
   "pron": "ben-ta-NI-ya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «ventana», but smaller. It is also the window of a car, train or plane.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "visado",
   "significado": "visa",
   "pron": "bi-SA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The v sounds like b: bi-SA-do. You apply for it («solicitar») at a consulate. Not every traveller needs one.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "plazo",
   "significado": "deadline; time limit",
   "pron": "PLA-tho",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You say «dentro del plazo» or «fuera de plazo». The z sounds «th»: PLA-tho.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "trámite",
   "significado": "procedure; formality",
   "pron": "TRA-mi-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent on the first a. In the plural, «trámites», the strong syllable does not change.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "caducar",
   "significado": "to expire",
   "pron": "ka-du-KAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is said of documents and food: «caduca el pasaporte». Something «caducado» (expired) is no longer good.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tasa",
   "significado": "fee; charge",
   "pron": "TA-sa",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You pay («pagar») a tasa for an official procedure. It is not «taza», the coffee cup: they sound different in Spain.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "rellenar",
   "significado": "to fill in",
   "pron": "rre-ye-NAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You fill in a form or a glass: you fill the empty spaces. The ll sounds like y.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "empadronarse",
   "significado": "to register as a resident",
   "pron": "em-pa-dro-NAR-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is signing up in your town hall's register. It is not the same as applying for a residence permit.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pase",
   "significado": "go in (pasar)",
   "pron": "PA-se",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Command for «usted»: -ar verbs end in -e. «Pase» invites someone in.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "rellene",
   "significado": "fill in (rellenar)",
   "pron": "rre-YE-ne",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive and «usted» command of «rellenar»: «que rellene».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "basta",
   "significado": "is enough (bastar)",
   "pron": "BAS-ta",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Basta con» + infinitive or noun means that is enough.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "presentar",
   "significado": "to show; to submit",
   "pron": "pre-sen-TAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You «presentar» a document or a complaint. It also means to introduce someone.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "traigas",
   "significado": "you bring (traer)",
   "pron": "TRAI-gas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Subjunctive of «traer». It comes from «traigo»: «hace falta que traigas».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "reciente",
   "significado": "recent",
   "pron": "rre-THYEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has one form for masculine and feminine: «foto reciente».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "previa",
   "significado": "prior; in advance",
   "pron": "PRE-bya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The v sounds like b. «Cita previa» is an appointment made before.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pitido",
   "significado": "beep",
   "pron": "pi-TI-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «pitar», to make a high short sound.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "casillas",
   "significado": "boxes; squares",
   "pron": "ka-SI-yas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Plural of «casilla». The «ll» sounds like y.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sella",
   "significado": "stamps (sellar)",
   "pron": "SE-ya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «sello», the stamp. The «ll» sounds like y.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "papeles",
   "significado": "papers; documents",
   "pron": "pa-PE-les",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Plural of «papel». It has no accent: «papeles».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "golpean",
   "significado": "they hit (golpear)",
   "pron": "gol-PE-an",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «golpe». Two strong vowels, e and a, split: gol-PE-an.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "terminado",
   "significado": "finished",
   "pron": "ter-mi-NA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Participle of «terminar», used as an adjective: «el trámite terminado».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "válido",
   "significado": "valid",
   "pron": "BA-li-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The v sounds like b and the accent marks the first syllable: BA-li-do.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "inscribirte",
   "significado": "to register yourself (inscribirse)",
   "pron": "ins-kri-BIR-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Infinitive with «te»: you register yourself, for example at the town hall.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  }
 ],
 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Necessary, or not",
     "texto": [
      "Official procedures always come with rules and requirements.\n\n- **Hay que** + infinitive expresses a general obligation: **Hay que pedir cita previa**. **Es necesario** + infinitive says the same: **Es necesario presentar el DNI**.\n- **Hace falta que** / **Es necesario que** + a conjugated verb takes the subjunctive: **Hace falta que traigas** una foto.\n- **No hace falta que** + subjunctive says something is optional, not forbidden: **No hace falta que vengas** in person.\n- **Basta con** + infinitive or noun says something is enough: **Basta con** rellenar este impreso.\n\nUsual steps: **solicitar** a visa, **renovar** the passport, **rellenar** a form, ask for **cita previa**, pay a **tasa** and hand in the papers **dentro del plazo**. A document **caduca** when its validity ends. **Empadronarse** is registering at the town hall where you live; it is not the same as applying for a residence permit."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Saying that something is necessary",
     "texto": [
      "There are three ways to say something is necessary:\n\n- **Hay que** + infinitive: the obligation applies to everyone. **Hay que pedir cita previa.**\n- **Hace falta que** / **Es necesario que** + subjunctive: the action belongs to a specific person. **Hace falta que traigas una foto.**\n- **No hace falta que** + subjunctive: it is not required, but it is not forbidden either. **No hace falta que vengas.**\n\nTo say something is enough, use **basta con** + infinitive or noun: **Basta con el DNI**, **basta con rellenar el impreso**."
     ],
